 "source_url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/Dfgoo2NSBo-/",
 "title": "Improve Critical Thinking",
 "topic": "communication",
 "summary": "The creator suggests that to become a better communicator, you must practice thinking alongside speaking by using the three whys technique. When given a statement, instead of instantly agreeing or disagreeing, you ask yourself three specific questions to examine your opinion, look for supporting evidence, and consider another perspective.",
 "key_points": [
  "To become a better communicator, practice thinking in addition to speaking.",
  "Use the three whys technique when given a statement like 'social media does more harm than good'.",
  "First question to ask yourself: Why do I believe this?",
  "Second question to ask yourself: What evidence or example supports my opinion?",
  "Third question to ask yourself: Could there be another side to this argument?",
  "This process ensures you do not just form an opinion, but examine it, look for supporting reasons, and consider another perspective."
 ],
 "content": "Learn #english #communication #learnenglish #publicspeaking #vocabulary Make a note of this post. One exercise to improve your critical thinking. Do you want to become a better communicator? Then don't just practice speaking, practice thinking as well. Here's a small exercise or a simple exercise I want to try. It's called three whys technique. Here's how it works. I'll give you a statement, let's say, social media does more harm than good. Most people will immediately agree or disagree. But instead of giving a quick opinion, ask yourself three questions. First, why do I believe this? Second, what evidence or example supports my opinion? Third, could there be another side to this argument? Now, you didn't just form an opinion, you examined it. Looked for supporting reasons and considered another perspective. That's how it works and it's very simple. Don't forget to follow English company for more interesting videos.",
